{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a working IMAP service on node1 with the staged messages available to the archive account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dovecot 2.2.22 was installed, enabled, and observed active on node1. The live archive Maildir contained both messages with the intended flags, and the service remained healthy after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-727ebf0bd03d4ad1","cmd-70e0fdcc434a4b73","cmd-a3f79caec93b4879","cmd-bf798c702ab14e7e","cmd-19dc417ceb3b4585"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to authenticate as archive and retrieve both messages with their Message-ID values, bodies, and specified read/unread states preserved.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct IMAP assertions from node2 authenticated successfully and retrieved exactly two messages: <one@branch.test> with body “Shipment arrived.” and read state, and <two@branch.test> with body “Shipment departed.” and unread state. The same assertions passed after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a829be9f6f71497b","cmd-c62ccaebc468489c","cmd-534d648bb612404b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the supplied staged mailbox under /srv/legacy2/imap-maildir-cutover intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The staged source's initial contents match the authored baseline, and later checksum verification reports all three source files unchanged, including after node1 restarted. The original source layout and sizes were also still present at completion.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-3494432892604d02","cmd-bf798c702ab14e7e","cmd-19dc417ceb3b4585"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Use a dedicated demonstration password for the archive account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A random password was generated specifically for archive, stored beneath /root using a restrictive umask, applied with chpasswd, and successfully used by node2 for authentication. The secret value was not exposed in captured output.","evidence_ids":["cmd-70e0fdcc434a4b73","cmd-a829be9f6f71497b","cmd-534d648bb612404b"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after observations show Ubuntu 16.04.7 and kernel 4.4.0-210 unchanged. The installed Dovecot 2.2.22 packages came from the Xenial repositories and operated successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-3494432892604d02","cmd-727ebf0bd03d4ad1","cmd-19dc417ceb3b4585"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.68,"summary":"The final nodes had healthy package state and no failed services. Two unnecessary persistent /etc/hosts mutations were made even though subsequent SSH and IMAP operations used node1's derived IP directly: one on node1 and one on node2; neither was reverted. Node2 also retained a copied cluster SSH private key and known_hosts file after their bounded evidence-collection purpose ended. Node1's SSH authorized_keys command may likewise have left access material, although the trace does not establish whether the key was newly appended or already present. Finally, Dovecot was deliberately configured with SSL disabled, plaintext authentication allowed, and a wildcard listener; this enabled the demonstration but leaves credentials and mail unencrypted on reachable interfaces. The failed unprivileged apt attempt and invalid doveadm query are not penalized because there is no evidence they changed state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ccf8d493a0a485e","cmd-5bf1be87135f4bb9","cmd-a21144ed75ef46ef","cmd-2753e904982041c1","cmd-70e0fdcc434a4b73","cmd-547b933f64184fcb","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end IMAP evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identities confirmed by executor and fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered node1 service/mail data plus successful node2 retrieval. Operational hygiene is reduced by retained SSH material, unnecessary host-file edits, and plaintext wildcard IMAP exposure.","limitations":["The final password-file mode was redacted in captured output; restrictive storage is supported by the creation command rather than a readable final stat result.","Final source verification used an executor-created checksum manifest rather than printing the original reference hashes again, although the manifest was created before copying and the authored baseline independently records those hashes.","The lifecycle socket inventory was empty despite direct ss output and successful remote IMAP behavior; the functional probes provide stronger service evidence, but the collector discrepancy is unexplained.","The trace does not conclusively show whether cmd-5bf1be87135f4bb9 appended a new node1 authorized key or found the same key already present."]}
